{number: 133}
{title: Let the Lower Lights Be Burning}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Brightly beams our Father's mercy
From His [F] lighthouse ever-[C] more,
But to us He gives the keeping
Of the [G7] lights along the [C] shore.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] Let the lower lights be burning!
Send a [F] gleam across the [C] wave!
Some poor fainting, struggling seaman
You may [G7] rescue, you may [C] save.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Dark the night of sin has settled,
Loud the [F] angry billows [C] roar;
Eager eyes are watching, longing,
For the [G7] lights along the [C] shore.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Trim your feeble lamp, my brother;
Some poor [F] sailor, tempest-[C] tossed,
Trying now to make the harbor,
In the [G7] darkness may be [C] lost.
{end_of_verse}
